To solve this problem, we need to determine how many 6-inch pieces can be obtained from a 4-foot wire. 

First, it's essential to convert the length of the wire into the same units as the length of the pieces. Since the pieces are 6 inches long and the wire is given in feet, we convert the wire length from feet to inches. There are 12 inches in a foot, so:
$$
4 \text{ feet} \times 12 \text{ inches/foot} = 48 \text{ inches}
$$

Now, we need to find how many 6-inch pieces can be cut from 48 inches. This is a division problem where we divide the total length by the length of each piece:
$$
48 \text{ inches} \div 6 \text{ inches/piece} = 8 \text{ pieces}
$$

Thus, Tracy obtained 8 pieces of wire.

