Cecilia needs to calculate the total amount of dog food required for the first year. The first 180 days require 1 cup of dog food per day, and the remaining 185 days (365 - 180) require 2 cups of dog food per day. 

Calculating the food for the first 180 days:
$$ 180 \text{ days} \times 1 \text{ cup/day} = 180 \text{ cups} $$

Calculating the food for the remaining 185 days:
$$ 185 \text{ days} \times 2 \text{ cups/day} = 370 \text{ cups} $$

Total dog food required for the year:
$$ 180 \text{ cups} + 370 \text{ cups} = 550 \text{ cups} $$

Each bag contains 110 cups, so the number of bags needed is:
$$ \frac{550 \text{ cups}}{110 \text{ cups/bag}} = 5 \text{ bags} $$

$$
\boxed{5}
$$
